# A finality counter replaces only a move from the battlefield to a graveyard (CR 122.1h; the ruling: "Finality counters
# don't stop permanents from going to zones other than the graveyard"). Bot2's Boomerang Basics returns Summon: Esper
# Maduin, with its finality counter, to its owner's hand: it goes there, as the card Esper Origins (front face, CR 712.8a),
# and nothing is exiled. Bot2 did not control it, so Bot2 draws nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Sol Ring
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Esper Origins
Island
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Boomerang Basics
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Esper Origins.Cast
Bot1.Arrange( | Island; Island)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Graveyard.Esper Origins.Cast(Ability: Flashback)
Bot1.Arrange(Lightning Bolt; Island | )
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Summon: Esper Maduin.Counters.Finality = 1
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Boomerang Basics.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Summon: Esper Maduin)
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Esper Origins
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Sol Ring; Mox Emerald
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
